  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This may seem small but if ~I~ can see it, I assume thousands of others of people will find this a bit odd or offputting.\nThe new avatar selection system has a change of verbage, from \"change\" to \"wear\", as in \"Wear these avatars\".\nFirst, I would like to suggest, if you're interested to changing to a different word, please try \"use\". \"Use these avatars\" is very neutral sounding.\nWhy I feel this way is simply when I think of \"wear these avatars\", I feel like the connotation is the avatars are no longer 'you', you're merely 'wearing' them. Like a sweater. Since VR's goal in general is to maximize immersion and pull you into the environment, this verbage does the opposite, reminding the user that this experience isn't real, you aren't a bug or a robot or an alien, and it's that pulling \"out\" of the experience, the reminder that it's all smoke and mirrors, kills it a bit. \nFurther, I start thinking of \"wearing a body suit\". Or \"wearing skin\", since you're essentially equipping what is akin to a \"fur suit\" when donning avatars. I'm sure even the furry community would prefer to \"use\" a furry avatar instead of \"wearing\" one. But mostly back to the \"wearing skin\" idea, bad connotations, don't like it.",
